 "api_error_status": null,
 "result": "Rules are recorded as deferred callbacks on the bundle, then replayed against the app at registration. All of this is in `src/tessel/sansio/bundles.py` unless noted.\n\n1. **Recording.** `Bundle.attach_route_rule()` (L413) doesn't touch an app. After checking that the endpoint and view names contain no dots, it calls `self.record(lambda s: s.attach_route_rule(...))` (L433). `record()` (L224) appends the lambda to `self.deferred_functions`.\n\n2. **Registration.** `App.register_bundle()` (`src/tessel/sansio/app.py:571`) calls `Bundle.register(app, options)` (L273).\n   - It computes the dotted name from `name_prefix` and `name`, and raises `ValueError` if that name is already taken.\n   - It stores the bundle in `app.bundles[name]` and builds a state with `make_setup_state()` (L246).\n   - It merges the bundle's handlers into the app via `_merge_bundle_funcs()` (L379).\n   - It runs each deferred callback with the state: `for deferred in self.deferred_functions: deferred(state)` (L334-335).\n\n3. **Applying.** `BundleSetupState.attach_route_rule()` (L87) is what each deferred lambda calls.\n   - It joins `url_prefix` onto the rule.\n   - It defaults `subdomain` from the state.\n   - It merges `url_defaults` into `defaults`.\n   - It prefixes the endpoint as `name_prefix.name.endpoint`.\n   - It then calls `self.app.attach_route_rule(...)`, the real app-level method (`src/tessel/sansio/app.py:606`).\n\nThe bundle's static route is added directly in `register()` (L323-328) through the same `state.attach_route_rule`.",
